WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.902 --> 00:00:09.849
A dozen agents in two projects, and more as the leaders hire.

2
00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:16.661
The ampersand opens the jump line: every agent and every project, the ones that need

3
00:00:16.661 --> 00:00:19.742
you first, each with what it is doing.

4
00:00:19.742 --> 00:00:26.230
A few letters of a name narrow it, a digit takes the nth at once, and enter goes

5
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.474
there, unfolding its project on the way.

6
00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:34.889
Let us pause the simulation, so the rows hold still.

7
00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:41.534
Enter opens its screen: the card and what it has cost, how full its context window

8
00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:48.341
is, how busy it was over the last two minutes, and its own to-do list, step by step.

9
00:00:48.341 --> 00:00:50.286
Below, its card's story.

10
00:00:51.486 --> 00:00:58.275
Capital K peeks instead: the same screen in a window over the salon, so you keep

11
00:00:58.275 --> 00:00:59.209
your place.

12
00:00:59.209 --> 00:01:03.537
j and k step from agent to agent; escape closes it.

13
00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:14.456
Capital F puts a letter on every row you can select: the agents, the items waiting

14
00:01:14.456 --> 00:01:16.854
for you, the lines of the journal.

15
00:01:16.854 --> 00:01:19.253
Type the letter and you are there.

16
00:01:19.253 --> 00:01:22.003
Type it as a capital, and it opens too.

17
00:01:31.823 --> 00:01:39.594
s settles the row at hand: it leaves the salon until it needs you again, and the

18
00:01:39.594 --> 00:01:43.188
salon's title counts what is settled.

19
00:01:43.188 --> 00:01:46.394
A row that needs you does not go.

20
00:01:46.394 --> 00:01:51.154
Colon unsettle, or the jump line, brings it back.

21
00:01:52.502 --> 00:01:54.948
Let the simulation run again.

22
00:01:54.948 --> 00:02:01.697
Your conversation with an agent is v from its row; here, the leader's reply to a

23
00:02:01.697 --> 00:02:02.372
request.

24
00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:09.375
Inside it, v chooses lines: j and k grow the choice, w and b go word by word, and y

25
00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:16.124
copies them as plain text, cleaned of anything that should not leave the screen.

26
00:02:16.124 --> 00:02:22.873
m marks a line to come back to with the apostrophe; marks are kept between runs.

27
00:02:32.781 --> 00:02:36.969
When a project's work is done, colon archive puts it away.

28
00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:42.890
For ten seconds, u still keeps it; then its agents go to sleep with their sessions

29
00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:47.873
and their mail, and a fresh project of the same name takes its place.

30
00:02:50.784 --> 00:02:54.788
Capital A lists the archives by checkout.

31
00:02:54.788 --> 00:03:02.503
Enter opens one as it was, read-only: its salon, its journal, what still waits.

32
00:03:02.503 --> 00:03:10.315
Escape comes back, and r restores it, asleep, while the fresh project gives way.

33
00:03:17.915 --> 00:03:21.927
And every key can be bound to one of your own, in a key file.

